WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.685
We say we want colleges to be more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.685 --> 00:00:04.809
equitable, more&nbsp;accessible.

00:00:05.272 --> 00:00:08.505
But we tend to obsess over a 
tiny group of colleges, 

00:00:08.505 --> 00:00:14.289
places like Harvard, Stanford,
 Yale, Princeton,&nbsp;MIT.&nbsp;

00:00:14.289 --> 00:00:17.723
But our cultural obsession with a limited group

00:00:17.723 --> 00:00:21.412
of&nbsp;highly rejective colleges
 has major consequences.

00:00:21.412 --> 00:00:25.384
Regional public universities,&nbsp;
or RPUs for short,

00:00:25.384 --> 00:00:27.323
are the exact opposite.

00:00:27.323 --> 00:00:32.965
RPUs, pride themselves on accepting 
everyone or almost everyone who applies.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:37.786
RPU students&nbsp;are more likely to be first 
generation college students like I was,

00:00:37.786 --> 00:00:41.902
students of color,&nbsp;low-income students, veterans.

00:00:41.902 --> 00:00:43.538
So when you hear someone saying,

00:00:43.538 --> 00:00:45.916
"Oh,&nbsp;anyone can get into that school,"

00:00:45.916 --> 00:00:48.133
push them on why that's a bad thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:50.113
You don't have to be rude about&nbsp;it.

00:00:50.113 --> 00:00:51.224
You could just say,

00:00:51.224 --> 00:00:54.000
"Wow, that's amazing

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.618
that that school gives so many&nbsp;people

00:00:56.618 --> 00:00:59.517
the opportunity to go to college."

